From f9f4a26d0b0ac428d8cb739512c3de65ab111516 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elieaazzam-art <elieaazzam-art@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:03:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(client): nine synthesized cues, the rate limiter,
 and the two-arm sink (sound.rs, PLAN-M10.2 4.2-4.4)

The Phase 4 sound module, wired live: CueBank synthesizes the nine cue
buffers at startup (mono 44100 Hz PCM, deterministic, all under a
second, pairwise distinct, soft-limited into the rail); RateLimiter
gives every cue its own 80 ms window (first passes, repeats inside
drop, the window reopens after - a big fight stays a heartbeat); Sound
is the App's sink behind the engine's AudioSink seam - the constructor
probes the device once (a /dev/snd pre-check keeps the no-device path
from waking libasound's chatty config parser: the fallback is
silent), a live device takes the rodio arm whose stream owner lives
for the App's whole lifetime, any failure or a mid-session device
loss takes the null arm (the engine's NullAudioSink counting what
would have played - never a panic, never a block, one honest startup
line).

The wiring (thin, in main.rs): the step's events still feed the sink
after the step (FD-9 order kept); an order submitted acknowledges on
the direct path (A-120: submitted, not non-rejected - the sim's
verdict surfaces separately); every user-driven selection change
funnels through one set_selection gate that cues the membership
change (A-122); every menu row activation funnels through one
menu_activate core that cues the UI click (A-121 - Enter, click, and
the end-screen R shortcut share it). The master volume row now drives
the sink live (A-115 semantics). The headless smoke constructs the
real sink (the probe runs, the null arm under CI), and the --frames
summary plus the smoke print what audio did: the arm and the cues'
fed/voiced/dropped fates - never a claim of audible sound on a
machine that cannot hear.

A-120..A-124 register the pass's guesses. 17 new tests: the bank
(short, distinct, deterministic, in-range), the limiter (window,
independence, reset), the fallback arm (no panic, the null-sink
oracle), the shared limiter across sources, the per-match reset, the
volume clamp, the evidence line, and the three wiring paths through
App (the null arm forced - the machine's probe result is never a
test input). All three goldens bit-identical.
