From b5404ce33abaa31cf7dab85a42f7e16c6003c5e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elieaazzam-art <elieaazzam-art@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:11:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(client): the mute setting joins the audio pass - the
 eighth key, row 5, wired live (PLAN-M10.2 4.4)

Mute is the eighth config key, right after master_volume: Settings,
SETTING_KEYS, to_text, the parser (a Phase 3 seven-key file parses with
mute off - the key is purely additive), adjust_setting (row 5), and
the settings screen's rows (fullscreen/debug_overlay shift to rows
6/7, Done to 8). Both keyboard and mouse reach the new row - the focus
map walks all nine buttons and the ui.rs button-id/focus tests pin
the match against the machine.

The semantics (A-125, carried live per A-115): mute beats volume and
never zeros it - the sink reads a muted flag as gain 0 whatever the
volume says, unmuting restores the set loudness, and the two rows
never write each other's value. Muting silences output, not evidence:
the cue counters keep counting. The evidence line says [muted] when
muted. The sink constructor now takes the loaded settings' volume and
mute, and adjust_setting drives set_volume/set_muted live.

DEBT-011 is repaid with this commit (the audible backend, the
synthesized bank, the limiter, the fallback, volume AND mute - the
whole sketch, on the standing seam); DEBT-015 closes with it (all
three deferred phases are built - what remains of A14 is the owner's
>=5-tester gate, not milestone scope). 3 new config tests (backward
compatibility, mute spellings + round-trip, the shifted row indices)
and 1 new sound test (mute precedence); the screens/ui/config row
pins all move to the nine-row layout. Total: 546 dev tests.
