Subject: [PATCH 5/5] docs: the M10.2 Phase 4 closeout - AI-Handoff (snapshot,
 counts, board, inventory, gotchas), CHANGELOG, README, PLAYTEST

The handoff's snapshot names the final gate (the owner's Phase 4
re-test on real hardware, then the A14 >=5-tester playtest), the test
counts (546 dev / 541 release expected), the status board flips to
all-four-phases complete, the workspace inventory gains sound.rs and
the seam's on_cue, and the gotchas record the Phase 4 lessons: the
rodio stream owner's lifetime (MixerDeviceSink is 0.22's OutputStream;
boxed in the arm; reset never re-probes; log_on_drop(false) is
load-bearing), the client-side cue path (on_cue not cue_for; the
limiter sits between the wiring and the arm; the null sink's counter
is the post-limiter oracle), the rate limiter's per-cue window, and
the cannot-hear rule (the /dev/snd pre-check keeps the fallback
silent; evidence lines claim counting, never sound).

The CHANGELOG carries the phase entry (scope, the exit bar, the
verification record). The README's badge flips to M10.2 done and the
status + client/engine bullets describe the audio pass. PLAYTEST
gains the Phase 3 re-test row (the owner's go, A-119) and the Phase 4
delivery note: the re-test is entirely about ears - the machine proved
wiring and counting; distinct, pleasant sound is the owner's call.
