 - **M10.2 Phase 3: XTEST driver discipline.** Keys sent faster than ~0.3 s apart can be processed against stale screen state under llvmpipe load (the first settings-persistence run "failed" because of a too-tight key cadence and a driver arg-order bug — the app was fine). Use ≥0.25–0.4 s per key, pass mode-specific CLI args BEFORE `Popen`, and verify the seed in the evidence lines (the smoke summary and the live match-ended line both print it). The graceful close (WM_DELETE_WINDOW ClientMessage, 32-bit data) exits the app cleanly with its exit-state line.
 
+- **M10.2 Phase 4: the rodio stream owner lives in the sink — dropping it silences everything.** `Sound`'s device arm owns `MixerDeviceSink` (rodio 0.22's stream owner — the `OutputStream` of older rodio docs is gone; the task vocabulary and the ADR both note the rename). It is boxed inside the arm enum (clippy's large-variant lint), constructed ONCE per run (the probe is startup-only, never per match), and dropped only when the App drops — `reset_match_state` calls `Sound::reset()` (counters + limiter windows), NEVER a fresh `Sound`. Its `log_on_drop(false)` is load-bearing: rodio's default drop notice prints to stderr, which the pass's no-spam rule forbids.
+
+- **M10.2 Phase 4: the client-side cues arrive through `on_cue`, NOT `cue_for` — and the limiter sits between the wiring and the arm.** CommandAck (fired in `submit_order` AFTER `host.submit`, meaning submitted-not-non-rejected — A-120; behind the spectate gate), SelectionClick (one `set_selection` gate every user-driven change funnels through — membership change only, A-122; the match reset bypasses it), and UiClick (one `menu_activate` core wrapping the machine's `activate_index` — Enter, mouse click, and the end-screen R shortcut all share it, A-121). The null arm's `NullAudioSink::client_cues` is the wiring oracle — it counts POST-limiter (the limiter sits between source and arm by design), so rapid-fire wiring tests use one call per fresh app, or the pre-limiter `Sound::client_cues` counter.
+
+- **M10.2 Phase 4: the machine cannot hear — evidence lines claim counting, never sound.** Under Xvfb/CI there is no audio device: `device_plausible()`'s `/dev/snd` pre-check short-circuits the probe BEFORE libasound wakes (its config parser chatters a stderr burst on card-less machines — A-124), the null arm counts, and every evidence line says the arm first ("active (rodio, 44100 Hz)" / "null fallback (no device)" [+ " [muted]"]) then the cues' fates (fed/voiced/dropped + client-side). "Sounds good" is only ever the owner's re-test claim. The rate limiter is 80 ms PER CUE (a fight's AttackLanded storm does not silence UnitLost), and the per-voice work after the limiter is one Vec clone + one channel send — the drop path is one array lookup.
